# Waveshare ESP32-S3-Touch-LCD-1.85B

ESP32-S3R8, 16MB flash, 8MB OPI PSRAM, ST77916 360x360 round panel over QSPI. Build with PlatformIO on the pioarduino Arduino-ESP32 3.x platform. The build reuses board id `lilygo-t-display-s3` (the module is the same); per-board pins live in `firmware/include/boards/ws185b.hpp`.

Environments: `kmj-ws185b` (HID only, CDC off) and `kmj-ws185b-debug` (HID plus CDC at 115200 so upload can auto-reset once KMJ is installed). `ARDUINO_USB_MODE=0` applies here too; do not use hardware CDC mode.

Reserved pins:

- LCD QSPI: CS GPIO21, PCLK GPIO40, DATA0-3 GPIO46/45/42/41, RST GPIO3
- Backlight: GPIO5, plain PWM (not the LilyGO pulse driver)
- Touch CST816S shares I2C: SDA GPIO11, SCL GPIO10, reset GPIO1, IRQ GPIO4, address 0x15
- BQ27220 battery gauge on the same I2C bus at 0x55; the bus also carries the QMI8658 IMU (0x6B), ES8311 (0x30), ES7210 (0x80), and PCF85063 RTC (0x51), none of which KMJ uses. Take the I2C lock in `hal/i2c_lock`.
- Speaker amplifier enable on GPIO9: hold low at boot.
- SD card uses the SDMMC controller (GPIO12-17), not the display SPI bus.

Buttons and navigation:

- GPIO0 (BOOT) is the home/wake button: it feeds the same `sample.home` path as the LilyGO touch home key. GPIO0 is a strapping pin only at reset; holding it during reset enters download mode as usual.
- The PWR button is a hardware power latch (long press 2 s cuts power). The firmware cannot read it.
- There is no touch home key on this panel; the round UI has no back button. BOOT (short press) and the swipe-right gesture both return home.

Flashing:

- While the board runs the stock Waveshare firmware it enumerates as `303a:1001` (USB-Serial/JTAG), where the 1200 baud bootloader reboot does nothing. Use `scripts/flash-ws185b.sh --first-flash` for that first upload; afterwards the `-debug` env auto-resets as usual.
- The release asset for this board is `KMJ_<version>_firmware_ws185b.bin` (flash at offset `0x0`).

The round UI layout is `firmware/src/logic/layout_round.hpp` and is checked by the native tests; visual results can only be confirmed on the device.
